// TODO: Should 'int' only be castable to integer types, not floating point types?
// This would solve this ambiguity problem, as then
// - `add(10, 20)` would reference the `add(i32, i32) -> i32` function
// - `add(10.0, 20.0)` would reference the `add(f32, f32) -> f32` function
// It is uncertain whether this would be considered the correct behaviour, though.
